meta {
  name: Import Branch Radiology Panels By Filter
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-radiology-panels/import-by-filter
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "search": "",
    "department": "",
    "category": "",
    "listId": "{{branchRadiologyPanelListId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  "Select all" import: materializes **every** Master Data radiology panel matching
  the given filters (the same search/classification filters as the import-picker's
  "Available to Add" listing) into the branch pricing list — no client-supplied id
  list. The backend re-resolves the matching set (excluding ids already in the
  target list) and imports all of them. Returns `{ copied, updated, skipped }`
  (`skipped` is always 0 for this route).

  Body (all optional):
  - `search` — case-insensitive match against name/code.
  - `department` / `category` — case-insensitive match against the respective
    classification **name**. (Panels have no sub-category, unlike radiology tests.)
  - `listId` — target `BranchRadiologyPanelList`; must belong to the caller's branch
    (404 `BRANCH_RADIOLOGY_PANEL_LIST_NOT_FOUND`). Omit to import into the branch's
    default **Walk-in** list (always ensured to exist first).

  Tenant + active branch come from the JWT (never the body). 400
  `ACTIVE_BRANCH_REQUIRED` if the JWT has no active branch. 404
  `MASTER_DATA_NOT_MAPPED_TO_BRANCH` if the branch has no master data.
}
